{"acceptance_length": 6.166666666666667, "acceptance_lengths": [3, 1, 14, 9, 1, 3, 2, 1, 1, 4, 1, 2, 2, 2, 3, 1, 4, 7, 2, 6, 1, 1, 1, 6, 8, 5, 4, 2, 16, 16, 16, 16, 16, 16, 12, 1, 16, 16, 1, 3, 1, 1, 1, 6, 7, 9, 15, 6, 7, 10, 5, 5, 13, 5], "accepted_draft_lengths": [2, 0, 13, 8, 0, 2, 1, 0, 0, 3, 0, 1, 1, 1, 2, 0, 3, 6, 1, 5, 0, 0, 0, 5, 7, 4, 3, 1, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 15, 11, 0, 15, 15, 0, 2, 0, 0, 0, 5, 6, 8, 14, 5, 6, 9, 4, 4, 12, 4], "allocated_memory_after_bytes": 32132079616, "allocated_memory_before_bytes": 32132062208, "benchmark": "gsm8k", "completion": "We are given that **Hannah needs to drink 100 ml of water for every 200 calories she burns**. So, we can calculate the total number of calories she burns and then determine how much water she needs to drink based on that.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Calculate calories burned from aerobics\n\n- Time spent: **2 hours**\n- Calories burned per hour: **500 calories/hour**\n\n$$\n\\text{Calories from aerobics} = 2 \\times 500 = 1000 \\text{ calories}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Calculate calories burned from running\n\n- Time spent: **1 hour**\n- Calories burned per hour: **600 calories/hour**\n\n$$\n\\text{Calories from running} = 1 \\times 600 = 600 \\text{ calories}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Total calories burned\n\n$$\n\\text{Total calories burned} = 1000 + 600 = 1600 \\text{ calories}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: Calculate water needed\n\n- Water needed: **100 ml per 200 calories**\n\n$$\n\\text{Water needed} = \\frac{1600}{200} \\times 100 = 8 \\times 100 = \\boxed{800} \\text{ ml}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### \u2705 Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{800} \\text{ ml}\n$$", "decode_seconds": 2.87980391504243, "draft_calls": 54, "event": "benchmark_row", "input_tokens": 96, "mapper_checkpoint_sha256": "3b41c22c14d18a082ef923b63019dd73686601f8fdb935580c02699811f6c07d", "method": "relay_base", "output_hash": "0aebfac8ad2879cf36bd2aa4d77fe646d44bc4ebe17b08456e94ec2817ee8abf", "output_tokens": 332, "peak_allocated_memory_bytes": 3228749158